/*
------------------------------------------------------------
Problem    : Container With Most Water
Platform   : LeetCode
Topic      : Two Pointers
Difficulty : Medium

Problem:
Given an integer array height where height[i] represents the
height of a vertical line, find two lines that together with
the x-axis form a container that can store the maximum amount
of water.

Return the maximum area of water that can be stored.

Approach:
We use the Two Pointer technique.

Initially, place one pointer at the start of the array and
another pointer at the end.

The area of the container is calculated using:

Area = width * minimum height of both lines

After calculating the current area, we move the pointer
having the smaller height because the shorter line limits the
amount of water.

Why does this work?

The width decreases after every move, so to increase the area,
we need to search for a taller boundary. Moving the taller
line cannot improve the result because the shorter line will
still decide the container height.

Algorithm:
1. Initialize two pointers:
   - left = 0
   - right = n - 1

2. Calculate the current water capacity.

3. Update the maximum area.

4. Move the pointer with smaller height.

5. Continue until both pointers meet.

Time Complexity : O(n)

Space Complexity : O(1)

------------------------------------------------------------
*/

class Solution {
public:
    int maxArea(vector<int>& height) {

        // Pointer starting from the left side
        int left = 0;

        // Pointer starting from the right side
        int right = height.size() - 1;

        // Stores the maximum water area found so far
        int max_water = 0;


        // Continue until both pointers meet
        while(left < right) {

            // Calculate width between two lines
            int width = right - left;


            // Container height is limited by the shorter line
            int container_height = min(height[left], height[right]);


            // Calculate current container area
            int area = width * container_height;


            // Update maximum area
            max_water = max(max_water, area);


            // Move the shorter line pointer
            // because it limits the possible maximum area
            if(height[left] < height[right]) {
                left++;
            }
            else {
                right--;
            }
        }


        // Return maximum amount of water container can store
        return max_water;
    }
};
